Z||000002||mbramble||06-26-2001||07:56 PM||||What year car are you adding them to??  If it's an 87-88 (and maybe 86) you just have to plug them in to the connector that is down behind the radio; driver's side.<P>For 85's that don't have the harness installed, here's the link to batboy's how-to thread: <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||DecadenceR||06-26-2001||09:09 PM||||Thanks a lot guys, I appreciate it.<BR>Actually, they're going into an 84.||||reg||1
Z||000004||qwikgta||06-26-2001||09:16 PM||||So if i get you correct with an 88 coupe all i need to do is plug them up, there is already wires for this.  I have a aux pod with no gauges, I have not located a set yet cause' i figured it would be a red a$$ to put them in.  Great, thanks<P>ROb<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents. <A HREF="http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html</A>  <A HREF="http://vafiero.com" TARGET=_blank>http://vafiero.com</A> <p>[This message has been edited by qwikgta (edited 06-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||06-27-2001||05:16 AM||||I don't think all '86s have the harness.  The Monkeymobile ('86 coupe) doesn't (?), but my GT does (of course).  I've always been under the impression that all '86 and up had the harness.  Easy way to check.  Pull your radio out.  You'll have a couple bundles of wiring.  Attached to either the HVAC wiring or the stereo wiring, there should be another plug, kinda squarish with 6 connectors.  If you see that (and nothing's plugged into it) all you have to do is mount the aux gauges, cut a hole in your dash, and run the aux gauge harness.<P>MM||||reg||1
